Parameterise the donor in theta, for G4 (M6a/M6b) and the atlas (M7).
====================================================================

Apply ONLY in the disposable clone, ONLY for the mutation and atlas runs:

    cd /home/user/donor-smoke
    git apply marketing_experimentation/repro/recast/theta-mutation.patch

Never in the reference clone, and never before M5b. The golden replay joins
on `effect_label`, so it must run against the unpatched donor.

This is a diff, not vendored source (D5: the donor has no licence).

VERIFIED, not illustrative
--------------------------
Generated by editing a scratch clone and taking `git diff`, then checked:

    git apply --check          clean against a pristine clone at 5133d37
    python -m py_compile       both plot files compile after applying
    Rscript parse()            generate_panels.R parses, 55 expressions
    theta_label()              0 -> null, 0.075 -> effect, 0.02 -> eff_p020,
                               -0.05 -> eff_m050, 0.15 -> eff_p150
    gallery selection          1 truth: inferred; several: REFUSES;
                               GALLERY_THETA set: selects that one

WHY IT IS A STRICT SUPERSET
---------------------------
With no new flags the patched generator produces byte-identical output:
theta 0.0 still labels "null", 0.075 still labels "effect". Only a theta
outside that pair gets a new label, so the patch cannot invalidate the
golden replay even if applied by accident.

WHAT EACH HUNK IS FOR
---------------------
1. generate_panels.R, --effect_sizes flag          -> G4 criterion 1
2. generate_panels.R, magnitude-bearing labels     -> the structural defect:
     effect_labels are directory names, so a second theta silently
     overwrites the first. Blocking for the atlas at M7. Resolution is one
     part in a thousand; a collision is an error, not a silent share.
3. analysis/plot_forest.py                         -> criterion 5 (D7)
     true_values / col_titles derived from the data's own true_att_pct, the
     same quantity the metrics layer already trusts, so figure and table can
     no longer disagree about what the truth was. This one generalises to
     any number of arms: it draws a column per label.
4. analysis/plot_ci_gallery.py                     -> criterion 5 (D7), and
     a THIRD coupling the static audit missed: load_results() filtered on
     `effect_label == "effect"`, a literal label that selects nothing once
     labels carry magnitude.

A CORRECTION TO AN EARLIER VERSION OF HUNK 4
---------------------------------------------
That hunk first replaced the label filter with `effect_pct != 0`. That is
correct for a two-arm run and WRONG for the atlas: with seven truths in one
results file it pools six of them and draws a single reference line through
all six. Replacing a hard-coded 7.5% with a hard-coded "anything but zero"
is the same defect wearing a hat, and it would have fired on the very run
the patch was written for.

The gallery draws one true-ATT line per cell, so it is meaningful for one
truth at a time and now says so: it infers the truth when exactly one
non-null effect size is present, refuses with the list when several are,
and takes GALLERY_THETA to choose. Refusing is the point -- the failure this
patch exists to fix was a figure that kept drawing confidently after its
assumption stopped holding.

The same correction was applied to our own `determinism_probe.py`, which had
acquired the identical `effect_pct != 0` selector.

Criteria 2, 4 and 6 need no patch -- see docs/donor-repro.md 5a.

